# =============================================================================
# Rust build output
# =============================================================================
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock is intentionally NOT ignored: Mark Time ships binaries, and
# current Rust guidance is to commit the lockfile for binary crates so builds
# are reproducible. Do not add Cargo.lock to this file.

# =============================================================================
# OS noise
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# =============================================================================
# Editor / IDE noise
# =============================================================================
.idea/
.vscode/*
# Keep shared editor settings (recommended extensions, formatter/task config)
# if the project ever adds them deliberately; unignore explicitly here.
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp

# =============================================================================
# Generated agent harness (see AGENTS.md "Workflow")
# =============================================================================
# Spec material lives in openspec/ and IS committed. The per-agent skills and
# slash commands that drive it are generated by `openspec init`, and are not
# committed: they are regenerable and agent-specific rather than project content.
.claude/
.codex/
.design-pipeline/

# =============================================================================
# Local environment / secrets
# =============================================================================
.env
.env.local

# =============================================================================
# Upstream data cache (see DATA-LICENSING.md)
# =============================================================================
# Some upstream-sourced datasets (exchange calendars, holiday tables, venue
# notices) may not be redistributed, per the data-licensing policy. Those are
# fetched at build or run time rather than vendored, and any local cache of
# that fetched data must stay untracked.
/data/cache/
.gstack/

# Next.js frontend dependencies and local compiler caches. The static export in
# web/out is intentionally tracked so the Rust binary can serve a fresh clone.
/web/node_modules/
/web/.next/
/web/*.tsbuildinfo

# Sentrux rules and their reviewed structural baseline govern this repository.
# The user-level Git ignore treats .sentrux as local by default; keep this project's
# architecture contract visible to every clone.
!.sentrux/
!.sentrux/rules.toml
!.sentrux/baseline.json
